# Training and competence templates (TECH 4, FI 1 training).

block training_signatures
sign tr_prepared | Prepared by | prepared | I prepared this record and it is complete and accurate.
sign tr_reviewed | Reviewed by | reviewed | I reviewed this record. | training.edit
sign tr_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve this record. | training.edit
end

block matrix_levels
note Levels: 0 not trained, 1 in training (supervised), 2 trained (works alone), 3 experienced (can solve problems), 4 can train others. Required is the level the role needs.
end

template training-matrix | Training Matrix | TRAINING
tags training matrix, competence, gaps
purpose Show, for a department or area, which people are trained on which documents and skills, against what their role requires, so gaps are visible and planned.
scope Departments, cells or work areas.
instructions List the people and, for each, the level reached on each item against the level required. Gaps are counted automatically. Review at every change of people, documents or processes.
workflow Maintained by the supervisor, reviewed monthly, approved.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section tm_scope | Scope | 3
f tm_department | Department | department | *
f tm_as_of | As of | date | *
f tm_owner | Owner | user | *
section tm_matrix | Matrix | 1
use matrix_levels
table tm_rows | People and items | 1
groups Person:2; Item:2; Level:3; Training:2
c tm_person | Person | user | *
c tm_role | Role | text
c tm_item | Document, course or skill | text | *
c tm_item_rev | Revision | text
c tm_required | Required | integer | * min=0 max=4
c tm_actual | Actual | integer | * min=0 max=4
c tm_gap | Gap | calc | {MAX(0, tm_required - tm_actual)}
c tm_trained_on | Trained on | date
c tm_due | Retraining due | date
rule tm_rows.tm_gap | greaterThan | 0 | #FDE7E9 | bold
f tm_entries | Entries | calc | {COUNTA(tm_rows.tm_item)}
f tm_gaps | Entries with a gap | calc | {COUNTIF(tm_rows.tm_gap, ">0")}
f tm_coverage | Coverage | calc | {IF(tm_entries > 0, (tm_entries - tm_gaps) / tm_entries * 100, 0)} dec=0 unit=%
f tm_retrain_overdue | Retraining overdue | calc | {COUNTIF(tm_rows.tm_due, "<" & tm_as_of)}
use training_signatures
end

template competency-matrix | Competency Matrix | TRAINING
tags competency matrix, competence
purpose Record the competencies each role needs (education, training, skills and experience) and assess each person against them.
scope Roles that affect product conformity and the effectiveness of the management system.
instructions Define the competencies for the role first. Assess each person with the evidence. Gaps are closed by training, mentoring or reassignment and re-assessed.
workflow Competencies defined, people assessed, gaps planned, reviewed annually.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section cm_role | Role | 3
f cm_role_name | Role | text | *
f cm_department | Department | department
f cm_assessor | Assessor | user | *
section cm_competencies | Competencies | 1
table cm_rows | Assessments | 1
c cm_person | Person | user | *
c cm_competency | Competency | text | *
c cm_type | Type | choice | * [Education; Training; Skill; Experience; Certification; Behaviour]
c cm_required | Required level | integer | * min=0 max=4
c cm_assessed | Assessed level | integer | * min=0 max=4
c cm_evidence | Evidence | text
c cm_gap | Gap | calc | {MAX(0, cm_required - cm_assessed)}
c cm_plan | Plan to close the gap | text
rule cm_rows.cm_gap | greaterThan | 0 | #FDE7E9 | bold
f cm_gaps | Gaps | calc | {COUNTIF(cm_rows.cm_gap, ">0")}
use training_signatures
end

template skills-matrix | Skills Matrix | TRAINING
tags skills matrix, flexibility, cross-training
purpose Show who can perform which operations at what level, so shifts can be staffed and cross-training planned to remove single points of dependence.
scope Production areas, cells and lines.
instructions Rate each person on each operation. The number of qualified people per operation shows where cover is thin. Plan cross-training where fewer than the target number are qualified.
workflow Maintained by the supervisor, reviewed monthly.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section sk_scope | Scope | 3
f sk_area | Area or line | text | *
f sk_target_cover | Target qualified people per operation | integer | * min=1
f sk_as_of | As of | date | *
section sk_matrix | Matrix | 1
use matrix_levels
table sk_rows | Operations | 1
groups Operation:1; People:6; Cover:2
c sk_operation | Operation | text | *
c sk_p1 | Person 1 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_p2 | Person 2 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_p3 | Person 3 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_p4 | Person 4 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_p5 | Person 5 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_p6 | Person 6 | integer | min=0 max=4
c sk_qualified | Qualified (level 2 or more) | calc | {COUNTIF(CELLS(sk_p1, sk_p2, sk_p3, sk_p4, sk_p5, sk_p6), ">=2")}
c sk_short | Short of target | calc | {MAX(0, sk_target_cover - COUNTIF(CELLS(sk_p1, sk_p2, sk_p3, sk_p4, sk_p5, sk_p6), ">=2"))}
rule sk_rows.sk_short | greaterThan | 0 | #FDE7E9 | bold
section sk_people | People | 3
f sk_person1 | Person 1 | user
f sk_person2 | Person 2 | user
f sk_person3 | Person 3 | user
f sk_person4 | Person 4 | user
f sk_person5 | Person 5 | user
f sk_person6 | Person 6 | user
f sk_thin | Operations short of cover | calc | {COUNTIF(sk_rows.sk_short, ">0")}
use training_signatures
end

template position-training-requirements | Position Training Requirements | TRAINING
tags position, role, training requirements, curriculum
purpose Define the training a position needs: the documents, courses and qualifications, when each must be completed and how often it is repeated.
scope Every position whose work affects quality.
instructions List each requirement with its due period from the start date and its renewal. New starters are assigned these requirements automatically when the position is set.
workflow Drafted by the manager, reviewed by training, approved, revised on change.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
section ptr | Position | 3
f ptr_position | Position | text | *
f ptr_department | Department | department
f ptr_owner | Owner | user | *
section ptr_requirements | Requirements | 1
table ptr_rows | Requirements | 1
c pr_item | Document, course or qualification | text | *
c pr_type | Type | choice | * [Document read and understood; Classroom course; On-the-job training; External course; Certification; Assessment]
c pr_due_days | Due within (days of start) | integer | * min=0
c pr_renewal_months | Renewal (months, 0 for none) | integer | min=0
c pr_mandatory | Mandatory before working alone | boolean
c pr_record | Course or document | record
f ptr_count | Requirements | calc | {COUNTA(ptr_rows.pr_item)}
f ptr_before_alone | Required before working alone | calc | {COUNTIF(ptr_rows.pr_mandatory, TRUE)}
use training_signatures
end

template training-curriculum | Training Curriculum | TRAINING
tags curriculum, course plan
purpose Define a structured curriculum: modules in sequence, with objectives, duration, method and how learning is assessed.
scope Curricula for roles, programmes and onboarding.
instructions List each module in the order taken, with its learning objective and assessment. Total hours are calculated.
workflow Drafted, reviewed, approved, revised.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
section cur | Curriculum | 2
f cur_name | Curriculum | text | *
f cur_audience | Audience | text | *
f cur_owner | Owner | user | *
f cur_objective | Overall objective | longtext | *
section cur_modules | Modules | 1
table cur_rows | Modules | 1
c cu_seq | Sequence | integer | * min=1
c cu_module | Module | text | *
c cu_objective | Learning objective | text | *
c cu_method | Method | choice | * [Classroom; E-learning; On the job; Self-study; Workshop; External]
c cu_hours | Hours | number | * min=0 dec=1
c cu_assessment | Assessment | choice | [Test; Practical demonstration; Observation; Sign-off; None]
total cu_hours | sum | Total hours
running cu_hours
f cur_hours | Total hours | calc | {SUM(cur_rows.cu_hours)} dec=1
use training_signatures
end

template qualification-matrix | Qualification Matrix | TRAINING
tags qualification matrix, certified operations
purpose Show who is qualified for operations and processes that need formal qualification (special processes, inspection, testing) and when each qualification expires.
scope Operations and processes that need qualified people.
instructions Record the qualification, its evidence and expiry for each person. Expired qualifications are highlighted; the person may not perform the operation until requalified.
workflow Maintained, checked monthly, reviewed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section qm_scope | Scope | 3
f qm_area | Area | text | *
f qm_as_of | As of | date | *
section qm_rows_section | Qualifications | 1
table qm_rows | Qualifications | 1
c qm_person | Person | user | *
c qm_process | Operation or process | text | *
c qm_method | Qualified by | choice | * [Practical test; Written test; External certification; Witnessed work; Experience record]
c qm_qualified_on | Qualified on | date | *
c qm_expires | Expires | date
c qm_status | Status | calc | {IF(ISBLANK(qm_expires), "Current", IF(DAYS(qm_expires, qm_as_of) < 0, "Expired", IF(DAYS(qm_expires, qm_as_of) <= 30, "Expiring", "Current")))}
c qm_evidence | Evidence | text
rule qm_rows.qm_status | equals | Expired | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule qm_rows.qm_status | equals | Expiring | #FFF4D6
f qm_expired | Expired | calc | {COUNTIF(qm_rows.qm_status, "Expired")}
use training_signatures
end

template training-assignment | Training Assignment | TRAINING
tags training assignment
purpose Assign training to people with a reason and a due date, and track completion.
scope Training assigned for new starters, changes, findings and development.
instructions State why the training is assigned. Each person completes and signs in the system; overdue assignments are escalated to the manager.
workflow Assigned, completed, verified, closed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section ta | Assignment | 2
f ta_item | Course, document or skill | text | *
f ta_record | Course or document | record
f ta_reason | Reason | choice | * [New starter; Document revision; Process change; Corrective action; Audit finding; Development; Retraining]
f ta_reason_record | Related record | record
f ta_due | Due | date | *
f ta_trainer | Trainer | user
section ta_people | People | 1
table ta_rows | People | 1
c tp_person | Person | user | *
c tp_completed | Completed on | date
c tp_status | Status | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(DAYS(tp_completed, ta_due)), IF(DAYS(tp_completed, ta_due) <= 0, "On time", "Late"), "Open")}
rule ta_rows.tp_status | equals | Open | #FFF4D6
f ta_total | People | calc | {COUNTA(ta_rows.tp_person)}
f ta_done | Completed | calc | {COUNT(ta_rows.tp_completed)}
use training_signatures
end

template training-attendance | Training Attendance | TRAINING
tags attendance, sign-in sheet
purpose Record attendance at a training session: the session, the trainer, the material used and each attendee.
scope Classroom, workshop and on-the-floor training sessions.
instructions Record the material and its revision. Each attendee confirms attendance with their own signature in the system or on the printed sheet.
workflow Session held, attendance recorded, assessments linked, closed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section session | Session | 3
f ts_title | Session | text | *
f ts_date | Date | date | *
f ts_hours | Duration (hours) | number | * min=0 dec=1
f ts_trainer | Trainer | user | *
f ts_material | Material and revision | text
f ts_location | Location | text
section attendees | Attendees | 1
table att_rows | Attendees | 3
c at_person | Attendee | user | *
c at_department | Department | department
c at_attended | Attended | boolean | *
c at_assessment | Assessment result | choice | [Passed; Not passed; Not assessed]
rule att_rows.at_assessment | equals | Not passed | #FDE7E9 | bold
f att_count | Attended | calc | {COUNTIF(att_rows.at_attended, TRUE)}
f att_hours | Training hours delivered | calc | {att_count * ts_hours} dec=1
use training_signatures
end

template training-assessment | Training Assessment | TRAINING
tags assessment, test, knowledge check
purpose Assess whether a trainee has learned what the training intended, with the questions or tasks, the marks and the pass mark.
scope Training that requires an assessment.
instructions Score each question or task. The result is calculated against the pass mark. A trainee who does not pass is retrained and reassessed.
workflow Assessed, scored, reviewed, retraining assigned where needed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section asmt | Assessment | 3
f as_trainee | Trainee | user | *
f as_course | Course | text | *
f as_date | Date | date | *
f as_assessor | Assessor | user | *
f as_pass_mark | Pass mark | percent | * min=0 max=100
section asmt_items | Questions and tasks | 1
table as_rows | Items | 1
c as_item | Question or task | longtext | *
c as_max | Marks available | number | * min=0
c as_scored | Marks scored | number | * min=0
total as_max | sum | Available
total as_scored | sum | Scored
section asmt_result | Result | 3
f as_total_max | Marks available | calc | {SUM(as_rows.as_max)}
f as_total | Marks scored | calc | {SUM(as_rows.as_scored)}
f as_pct | Score | calc | {IF(as_total_max > 0, as_total / as_total_max * 100, 0)} dec=0 unit=%
f as_result | Result | calc | {IF(as_pct >= as_pass_mark, "PASS", "NOT PASSED")}
rule as_result | equals | NOT PASSED | #FDE7E9 | bold
use training_signatures
end

template on-the-job-qualification | On-the-Job Qualification | TRAINING
tags on-the-job, OJT, qualification
purpose Qualify a person to perform an operation on their own after supervised practice, with the tasks demonstrated and the trainer's and supervisor's sign-off.
scope Operations that require on-the-job training before working alone.
instructions The trainee performs each task under supervision the number of times required. The trainer records each demonstration. The supervisor verifies before the person works alone.
workflow Training started, tasks demonstrated, trainer sign-off, supervisor verification.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization after the person leaves the role.
section ojt | Qualification | 3
f oj_trainee | Trainee | user | *
f oj_operation | Operation | text | *
f oj_instruction | Work instruction and revision | text | *
f oj_trainer | Trainer | user | *
f oj_start | Started | date | *
section ojt_tasks | Tasks | 1
table oj_rows | Tasks | 1
c oj_task | Task | text | *
c oj_required | Demonstrations required | integer | * min=1
c oj_done | Demonstrations done | integer | min=0
c oj_ok | Complete | calc | {IF(oj_done >= oj_required, "Yes", "No")}
rule oj_rows.oj_ok | equals | No | #FFF4D6
f oj_open | Tasks not complete | calc | {COUNTIF(oj_rows.oj_ok, "No")}
sign oj_trainer_sign | Trainer | performed | I trained this person and observed each task demonstrated as recorded.
sign oj_trainee_sign | Trainee | prepared | I received this training and can perform these tasks.
sign oj_supervisor_sign | Supervisor verification | verified | I verified this person can perform the operation without supervision. | training.edit
end

template supervisor-verification | Supervisor Verification | TRAINING
tags supervisor verification, competence check
purpose Record the supervisor's verification that a trained person applies the training correctly in their actual work.
scope Training that requires verification of application at work.
instructions Observe the person at work after training. Record what was observed against each point.
workflow Observed, recorded, verified.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section sv | Verification | 3
f sv_person | Person | user | *
f sv_training | Training verified | text | *
f sv_date | Date observed | date | *
section sv_points | Points observed | 1
table sv_rows | Points | 1
c sv_point | Point | text | *
c sv_result | Result | choice | * [Applied correctly; Applied with coaching; Not applied]
c sv_note | Note | text
rule sv_rows.sv_result | equals | Not applied | #FDE7E9 | bold
f sv_not | Not applied | calc | {COUNTIF(sv_rows.sv_result, "Not applied")}
f sv_outcome | Outcome | calc | {IF(sv_not = 0, "Verified", "Retraining needed")}
sign sv_supervisor | Supervisor | verified | I observed this person at work and recorded what I saw. | training.edit
end

template certification-register | Certification Register | TRAINING
tags certification, register, expiry
purpose Register certifications held by people (internal and external), with the issuer, the reference and the expiry, so renewals are planned.
scope Certifications required by roles, customers or regulations.
instructions Record each certification with its evidence. The status is calculated from the expiry date.
workflow Maintained, checked monthly, reviewed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization after expiry.
landscape
section cr_scope | Register | 2
f cr_as_of | As of | date | *
f cr_owner | Owner | user | *
section cr_rows_section | Certifications | 1
table cr_rows | Certifications | 1
c cr_person | Person | user | *
c cr_certification | Certification | text | *
c cr_issuer | Issuer | text
c cr_reference | Reference | text
c cr_issued | Issued | date
c cr_expires | Expires | date
c cr_status | Status | calc | {IF(ISBLANK(cr_expires), "No expiry", IF(DAYS(cr_expires, cr_as_of) < 0, "Expired", IF(DAYS(cr_expires, cr_as_of) <= 60, "Renew", "Valid")))}
rule cr_rows.cr_status | equals | Expired | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule cr_rows.cr_status | equals | Renew | #FFF4D6
f cr_expired | Expired | calc | {COUNTIF(cr_rows.cr_status, "Expired")}
f cr_renew | Due for renewal | calc | {COUNTIF(cr_rows.cr_status, "Renew")}
use training_signatures
end

template qualification-register | Qualification Register | TRAINING
tags qualification, register, auditors, inspectors
purpose Register people qualified for roles that need formal approval (auditors, inspectors, testers, approvers), with their scope and the basis of approval.
scope Roles that the organization approves people for.
instructions Record the scope of each approval precisely. Approvals are reviewed at the interval set and withdrawn when the basis no longer holds.
workflow Approved, registered, reviewed, withdrawn when needed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization after withdrawal.
section qr | Register | 1
table qr_rows | Qualified people | 1
c qr_person | Person | user | *
c qr_role | Role | choice | * [Internal auditor; Lead auditor; Supplier auditor; Inspector; Tester; Calibration technician; Approver; Trainer; Other]
c qr_scope | Scope | text | *
c qr_basis | Basis of approval | text | *
c qr_approved_on | Approved on | date | *
c qr_review_due | Review due | date
c qr_status | Status | choice | * [Active; Suspended; Withdrawn]
rule qr_rows.qr_status | in | Suspended,Withdrawn | #EEEEEE
use training_signatures
end

template retraining-record | Retraining Record | TRAINING
tags retraining, refresher
purpose Record retraining given because of a revision, a lapse, an error or a finding, and confirm the person is competent again.
scope Retraining for any reason.
instructions State the trigger and link the record. Retraining is verified the same way as the original training.
workflow Triggered, retrained, verified, closed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section rtr | Retraining | 2
f rt_person | Person | user | *
f rt_item | Training | text | *
f rt_trigger | Trigger | choice | * [Document revision; Qualification lapse; Error or nonconformance; Audit finding; Periodic refresher; Return from absence]
f rt_trigger_record | Related record | record
f rt_date | Retrained on | date | *
f rt_trainer | Trainer | user
f rt_method | Method | choice | [Classroom; On the job; Read and understood; E-learning]
f rt_result | Result | choice | * [Competent; Further training needed]
rule rt_result | equals | Further training needed | #FFF4D6 | bold
use training_signatures
end

template training-effectiveness-review | Training Effectiveness Review | TRAINING
tags training effectiveness, evaluation
purpose Evaluate whether training achieved its purpose by comparing a performance measure before and after, and decide on further action.
scope Training programmes and significant individual training, as the organization decides.
instructions Choose a measure linked to the training purpose before training. Measure after enough time has passed. The change is calculated.
workflow Measure set, training delivered, measured after, decision recorded.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section te | Training | 2
f te_training | Training | text | *
f te_purpose | Purpose of the training | longtext | *
f te_measure | Measure | text | *
f te_higher_better | Higher is better | boolean
f te_before | Before | number | * dec=3
f te_after | After | number | dec=3
f te_change | Change | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(te_after), te_after - te_before, "")} dec=3
f te_change_pct | Change | calc | {IF(AND(ISNUMBER(te_after), te_before <> 0), (te_after - te_before) / ABS(te_before) * 100, "")} dec=1 unit=%
f te_improved | Improved | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(te_after), IF(te_higher_better, IF(te_after > te_before, "Yes", "No"), IF(te_after < te_before, "Yes", "No")), "")}
f te_decision | Decision | choice | [Effective; Partly effective - more training; Not effective - redesign]
rule te_improved | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
use training_signatures
end
